# kernel-patch-manifest: upstream tracking for Minime's kernel patch series.
#
# Each section names one patch file under minime/boards/<board>/patches/linux/
# followed by "upstream=<value>". This file is the single source of truth for
# patch triage: as kernel patches land in mainline, mark the section
# "upstream=master" (content confirmed in linux.git master) so it can be dropped
# on the next manual kernel bump.
#
# Values:
#   upstream=-          keep; content not (yet) confirmed upstream
#   upstream=master     content confirmed in linux.git master; auto-dropped on
#                       the next kernel bump (any bump pulls in a release that
#                       contains master)
#   upstream=<version>  confirmed in a specific mainline release; dropped once
#                       the pinned kernel reaches that version (not yet wired)
#
# All other keys are ignored. Do not add prose here beyond this header.

